Simon - both good questions, and both have clean answers!

1. The increase is real, not a double count. Ivan's team brought the packaging-cell sensors online on August 11, and from that date the cell contributes roughly 6.1M events a month on its own. Strip that out and the rest of the line is within two per cent of July. Yuki double-checked the connector update on the twelfth this morning and the dedupe on the event IDs is doing its job, so nothing is being counted twice. I've asked Yuki to add a "new sources this month" line to the report going forward so this is obvious at a glance.

2. Correct - the two extra seats are Yuki's and Mateo's support logins. They're flagged as vendor seats in our system and they are not billable, never have been. Your licensed count is twelve, your billed count is twelve. I'll get Kim to add a footnote to the next report so the number Walter sees matches the order form.

Unrelated, but since you mentioned onboarding: Yuki tells me the line 1 dashboards are now being used by the shift leads directly, not just by ops management. That's exactly the pattern we see at our happiest customers, so if there's ever appetite for a short training session for the shift leads, say the word.

Tomás

